  "notes": "Source: official DiGiCo S21 Datasheet (manufacturer PDF, digico.biz). Physical dims 763x586x295mm desktop console — no rackUnits set. Power: \"90-264 VAC, 47-63Hz Auto Sensing, 208 watts, 232VA\" via \"1 x PSU\"; exact IEC inlet variant (C13/C14) is not spelled out in the datasheet, so IEC is inferred (standard for this class of gear). AES/EBU In/Out are single XLR connectors each carrying a 2-channel (stereo) AES3 signal, modeled with connector \"aes3\" to distinguish from the analog mic/line XLRs. GPI/GPO are 1/4\" jacks, modeled as ts-6.35 (contact-closure, not audio TRS). The 24 Mic/Line inputs and 12 Line outputs are only given as aggregate counts on the rear panel (no individual factory labels), so they are enumerated generically as \"Mic/Line In 1-24\" / \"Line Out 1-12\". 2 x DMI expansion slots (up to 64 I/O each, accepting Dante/MADI/AES/Analog/Waves/Hydra2/etc. cards) exist on the rear panel but are omitted as fixed ports since their connector type depends entirely on the DMI card installed. Ethernet port speed (100M/1G) is not stated in the datasheet, so grade is omitted. The \"UB MADI\" USB-B port is very likely USB 2.0 (same generation as the console's other explicitly-labeled \"USB 2.0\" slots) but the datasheet does not state a version for this specific port, so grade is omitted there too. Front worksurface also has a USB 2.0 slot plus 1/4\" and 3.5mm headphone jacks, included alongside the rear I/O.",
